    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, or Scimitar), Rare (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>Thayan Swords are often awarded to premier Thayan knights when they complete their training.</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Knight of the Arcane.</strong> The sword has 4 charges and regains 1d4 charges daily at dawn. While holding the sword, you can expend 1 charge to cast one of the following spells (save DC 15):</p><ul><li><p>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSearingSmi]{Searing Smite}</p></li><li><p>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.spells.Item.hWuxMbikbMf0O5Ix]{Thunderous Smite}</p></li><li><p>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.spells.Item.TZSVMNFj00ubd60B]{Wrathful Smite}</p></li></ul><p><strong>Resurgent Warrior.</strong> If you’re reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright while holding this sword, you can drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-6tku1rrOawbpgpjp\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Glissez l’enchantement sur l’arme voulue : elle garde son nom, sa rareté et son prix. Elle reçoit le bonus de +1, 4 charges (1d4 à l’aube) et les trois sorts. <em>Thunderous Smite</em> et <em>Wrathful Smite</em> viennent du compendium Spells. <em>Resurgent Warrior</em> rend 1 point de vie.</p></section><p>@Embed[Compendium.dnd5e.content24.JournalEntry.dmgFoundryRefere.JournalEntryPage.Ok4iCgD25ENgoRxE cite=false caption=false classes=\"hide-in-embed\"]</p>",
